      "terminal_teaching": {
        "prerequisite_note": "After command search/permissions and current-file handover: use cat, cp and rm on ordinary virtual files. Here, learn to locate separate program artifacts without confusing a pathname with a current release.",
        "concepts": [
          {
            "title": "One application has several kinds of files",
            "text": "The program file, its manual and its source serve different purposes. which checks eligible external commands in the supplied PATH; whereis names files in a selected category. Neither action runs the program here. A found filename does not prove that its contents are current."
          },
          {
            "title": "Read the query and its result",
            "text": "In whereis -m -M /gallery/man -f democtl, -m selects manuals, -M gives the folder, and -f ends the folder list before the program name. Use -b/-B for the binary and -s/-S for source. A result starts democtl: followed by a path. A bare democtl: means no matching name in that folder; the normal query still exits successfully."
          },
          {
            "title": "Inspect the release before copying",
            "text": "The worked release note approves release 3. Read it with cat, then compare staged and published files. The gallery manual is absent under the exact democtl.1 name; its existing source has release 1. cp places a current file at the required destination. rm removes only the explicitly retired manual; preserve the archive and neighboring audit files."
          },
          {
            "title": "Verify the handover, not only the lookup",
            "text": "Repeat category discovery after editing, and cat the published source/manual. whereis cannot tell an archived release from a current one with the same name. Check work in the assignment checks names, complete file contents and preservation. help and show are simulator references; files are never executed."
          }
        ],
        "example": [
          "whereis -b -B /gallery/bin -f democtl",
          "whereis -m -M /gallery/man -f democtl",
          "cat /gallery/stage/release.txt",
          "cp /gallery/stage/democtl.1 /gallery/man/democtl.1",
          "cp /gallery/stage/democtl.c /gallery/source/democtl.c",
          "rm /gallery/man/democtl-old.1",
          "whereis -m -M /gallery/man -f democtl",
          "cat /gallery/source/democtl.c"
        ],
        "inputs": "Worked setup: democtl already has its binary in /gallery/bin. Its correctly named manual is missing, and the published source is release 1. /gallery/stage/release.txt approves release 3; /gallery/archive retains release 1.",
        "try_change": "After the worked repair, copy /gallery/archive/democtl.c over /gallery/source/democtl.c. Run whereis -s -S /gallery/source -f democtl, then cat that file: its path still appears but the content is old. Restore the staged source and read it again.",
